turning now overseas to an amazing  explosion of public anger in sri lanka  the island country off the southern  coast of  india it has forced the president and  prime minister to resign there as tens  of thousands of protesters occupied the  homes the bedrooms even the bathrooms of  two leaders in that country in the  capital city of colombo the country's  economy has collapsed it's run out of  food and fuel and medicine and other  essential supplies and as elizabeth  palmer reports the capital is now in  chaos  by saturday the pressure on the  government was overwhelming with tens of  thousands protesting outside the  presidential headquarters  and then as word spread that the  president had gone  a crowd surged into gautabaya  rajapaska's private residence and were  amazed  whole families toured the opulence  some tried out his private gym others  took a dip in the presidential pool  while security services stood back and  watched  the mood was festive  unlike the night before when police  fired tear gas  to disperse crowds who'd set fire to the  house of the prime minister  anger has been building over fuel  shortages and a collapsed economy thanks  in part to corruption and incompetence  but also to covet which shut down  tourism sri lanka's main source of  income  the protesters say they're going nowhere  until they're sure the president has  stepped down supposedly on wednesday  though there's been no word from the man  himself  apart from the fire the atmosphere has  remained largely peaceful and now  politicians are trying to build a  cross-party coalition to take power and  come to grips with the economic mess  vlad  liz thank you very much
 

